    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4105" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄληπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not to be laid hold of, hard
				to catch</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sert.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.169
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τοῖς ἐχθροῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					5.8.11
				</span></i>
			: in 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀληπτότερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				82
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				143
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>incomprehensible</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.54K.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Nic.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in Stoic
			philos., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄληπτα, τά</span>, things <i>not to be made matter of
			choice</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληπτά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.34
			</span></i>.</div>
